# Functional-identifier allowlist for the global pre-commit attribution guard.
#
# Mechanism approved 2026-07-03. A path listed here may contain external
# vendor/tool NAME strings when they appear as functional identifiers: real
# directory paths, settings filenames, hook event names, CLI invocations.
#
# Why this repository needs it:
#   FAVL Engineering OS is a policy layer for an external agent CLI. Its whole
#   purpose is to place files at that tool's real configuration paths
#   (~/.claude/, /etc/claude-code/, .claude/settings.json) and to describe the
#   hook events it dispatches. Those literal strings cannot be paraphrased
#   without making every install script and policy document wrong.
#
# What this does NOT relax. On every path listed here the guard still blocks:
#   * co-author trailers
#   * origination and "produced-with" notes
#   * attribution, contributor, credit, maintainer and acknowledgement lines
#     naming anyone other than Frank Asante Van Laarhoven
#
# So Article VII of constitution/CONSTITUTION.md stays enforced by the same
# hook that would otherwise reject these files.
#
# Scope is per-path, not repository-wide. VERSION, LICENSE, NOTICE,
# .env.example and the src/ and tests/ placeholders are deliberately absent
# and are still scanned for vendor names.

.attribution-allow
.gitignore
CLAUDE.md
README.md
constitution/*
standards/*
governance/*
docs/*
scripts/*
templates/*
.claude/*
.github/*
